  "predicted_delta_text": "**Prediction**: s11_db improves by ~4.0 dB.  \n*Reasoning*: The input node (n2) is currently connected to NM1 gate via R2 and to PM1 gate via R4. The lack of a proper input matching network causes the input impedance to be poorly matched. Introducing L3 (inductor) between n2 and n3 (which are both gate nodes) forms a **series resonant loop** with C2 (between n2 and n3). This creates a tuned input network: L3 + C2 resonates at 915 MHz, creating a low-impedance path at f0 that effectively shunts the input to ground at resonance, improving input match. The inductor L3 is placed between the two gate nodes, forming a loop that enhances the real part of the input impedance toward 50\u03a9. This is a classic technique in narrowband LNAs \u2014 using a resonant gate loop to achieve impedance matching. The structure is fully passive and adds no biasing complexity, making it a clean structural fix. The improvement is expected to be significant due to resonant input tuning.",
